Only these route-local modules plus report-level claims explicitly marked canonical in `docs/state/theorem-state.yaml` are canonical Target C theorem sources at audit.66. Sections 110--121 are canonical report-level entries and are linked below. The exact train-coupled floor endpoint exclusion is also canonical; its detailed proof and independent audit are linked below. The file `95-protected-contact-creation-obstruction-audit.md` remains proof-only and is intentionally outside the canonical reading order.

## Scope rule

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`, not the full source:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Do not extend the affine-kernel conclusion to their coordinates.

## Current route

Audit.64 retains the complete audit.52--63 stack, including terminal O--O depletion, and adds exact finite contact-budget and low-contact packet-opening endpoints.

Audit.65 adds the odd-shell blocker-payment theorem and an exact nonglobal-family regression. For regular odd `q>=65`, each strict interior contact isolate blocks at most one adjacent wall side, so fully blocking the inward one-vertex proposals requires at least `(q+1)/2` isolates. The constructed blocked quadratic filling is strictly beaten by a whole-source packet; this does not yield arbitrary-container capacity or change the C-II endpoint.

Audit.66 adds a collective exterior shield for a pairwise-distance-at-least-two set of deleted wall vertices, and a greedy `ceil(M/25)` bank from `1`-separated wall vertices. The finite replacement implication is subsumed by Audit.64. An exact D(8) heptagon-plus-center source shows that the wall-safe region can have capacity one even at a global minimizer; the capacity obstacle therefore needs a genuinely asymptotic canonical hypothesis.

Audit.61 reduces a sufficiently small O–O motion to
\[
\boxed{
\text{old diameter constraints}
+\ |J|\le d_H\text{ inactive upper exceptions}
+\ \text{unary rhombus tests}
+\ \text{outer-face near-unit pairs}.
}
\]

Audit.62 makes the remaining near-unit geometry substantially more ordered.

Canonical \`C-LOADED-NEAR-UNIT-ADJACENCY\` gives
\[
\tau_D=\frac{3D}{\sqrt{3D^2+4}+1}
\]
and proves that every nonconsecutive loaded pair \(a,b\) with \(|ab|<D\) satisfies
\[
|ab|\ge\tau_D.
\]
For \(D\ge6\), every loaded pair of length at most \(13/12\) is therefore a loaded-hull side. The loaded near-unit conflict graph is a subgraph of the loaded hull cycle and has maximum degree two.

Canonical \`C-LOADED-HULL-CAP-BUDGET\` controls geometry outside and near the loaded hull. With
\[
W=\operatorname{per}(\operatorname{conv}A)-q,
\]
occupied loaded-hull caps are at most \(W\), their total outer/base length is at most \(2W\), short core-to-exterior attachments are supported on at most \(68W\) core vertices, the nonloaded \(1/2\)-boundary layer inside the loaded hull has size at most \(12W\), and extreme source vertices outside the loaded set are at most \(W\). Deep loaded-hull interior points have an exact \(D-1/2\) upper margin.

Since canonical full-source geometry gives
\[
\operatorname{per}(\operatorname{conv}A)<\pi D,
\]
every subsequence with \(q/D\to\pi\) has \(W=o(D)\). Thus loaded-hull cap/exterior blockers are sublinear in the terminal regime.

Audit.63 narrows the live full-core branch: when q/D -> pi and u_B=o(D), no linear O--O stopped-train bank remains, and distinct narrow-window binary loaded witnesses number at most u_B. Any remaining linear obstruction must use face-coupled outer-to-bounded or bounded-to-bounded trains, unary rhombus tests, or the at most d_H inactive upper exceptions, while meeting all source lower and actual-diameter upper constraints.

The one-vertex shield retains contact isolates and excludes strict one-site activation in canonical unit hexagons; it does not yield general packet capacity.

The regular-shell barrier payment and strict sub-diameter whole-source competitor are recorded in the [Audit.65 independent audit](../../audits/target_c_odd_shell_barrier_payment_independent_audit_2026-10-06.md). They constrain that explicit shell family and do not close the macroscopic-container branch.

The [Audit.66 collective wall audit](../../audits/target_c_collective_wall_capacity_independent_audit_2026-10-06.md) retains exterior isolates under separated multi-vertex deletions, but proves no packet capacity for large chambers.

Audit.64 requires every finite exchange to count all inserted-to-retained contacts and actual diameter pairs. With strict upper slack, one or two new unit contacts can be opened, so a packet that removes an old contact must create at least three new contacts unless it also removes an actual diameter pair or strictly improves diameter.

The audit.61 regressions remain binding:

- arbitrarily small contact-preserving motion can still break a unary rhombus diagonal;
- a source path forest can become cyclic after contraction to owner labels.

The live full-core target is now a source-realized **face-coupled finite-move theorem**. A linear O--O train supply is unavailable in the terminal q/D -> pi, u_B=o(D) regime, and narrow-window binary loaded witnesses cost at most u_B. The remaining endpoint must use outer-to-bounded or bounded-to-bounded trains, explicit unary rhombus tests, or at most d_H inactive upper exceptions, while meeting every full-source lower and actual-diameter upper constraint.

The macroscopic-container branch remains separate.

